  "auroc": "Mann-Whitney AUROC for detecting worst-decile-rel-L2 cases. The positive-class threshold is the FULL-SAMPLE top-decile threshold and is held FIXED across bootstrap draws, so 'worst-decile case' is a property of the case (the paper's estimand) and the paired delta is not contaminated by label churn.",
  "spearman": "case-level Spearman(score, rel_L2).",
  "risk": "retained mean rel-L2 after rejecting the highest-scoring 10% of cases. Primary paired risk statistic because it is a difference of well-behaved means; oracle-recovery is a RATIO of differences whose denominator can approach zero under resampling, so it is reported as a descriptive on the full sample only.",
  "bootstrap": "10000 case-level resamples, seed 0, percentile CI."
 },
